      "writtenOn": "2023-12-18T12:34:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the BoringSSL implementation, this could end up [returning the result of `strerror`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/boringssl/src/crypto/err/err.c;l\u003d492;q\u003dstrerror), which worries me slightly -- `strerror` results are allowed to change under your feet.\n\nThe [man page](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/strerror.3.html) indicates that it should only change if there\u0027s another call to `strerror` (or `strerror_l`) in between getting the pointer and using it, so it\u0027s *probably* OK.\n\nBut maybe do the `.to_string_lossy()` in here so the reference doesn\u0027t hang around?",
      "revId": "b8bc0f9018ad9f277f07cefdb3555fda94c5e602",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
