      "message": "Ah, this doesn\u0027t actually help with my concern, but that\u0027s mostly because I misunderstood what `.to_string_lossy()` does -- I assumed it would alloc-and-copy the string, but it doesn\u0027t -- in either case (before/after), the output is a pointer to a C string that the spec says can change.",
